    "source": "sharegpt",
    "why": "Two generative tenants, and the HIGHEST-POWER scenario in the matrix. T1 established that MPS is bounded by power, not contention: every arm holding the 7B sat at 343 W of a 350 W board limit and MPS returned +0.0%, where round one at 249-256 W returned +24.9%. Three predictions registered before the run. (a) MPS again returns ~0%: adding a 1.5B to a card already at its ceiling cannot create headroom. (b) Sharing costs MORE than T1's +3.1% e2e p99, because the neighbour is a steady decode consumer rather than a bursty encoder. (c) The clock-residency gain that made bge-m3 7.4% FASTER will NOT appear for llm2 -- it only existed because the embedder alone left the card at 3.5% utilisation and 1,665 MHz. A 1.5B alone will already hold clocks near peak, so there is nothing for a neighbour to recover. T4 is the opposite extreme and the real test of the power hypothesis. OUTCOME (2026-09-02): the first attempt was VOID -- the MPS daemon was left up for every arm, so hami and hami-mps were the same configuration. Re-run with per-arm daemon control returned pooled time-in-system -26.7%, 7B -44.6%, 1.5B +24.2%. Power was never the mechanism; contention is. See FINDINGS 6."
  },
